# Cloudflare Pages reads this file at deploy time and does not serve it.
#
# The web build is a single-page app: expo-router owns /dish/…, /place/… and the
# rest on the client, and the export emits exactly one index.html. Without this
# line every URL except / returns 404 on a hard refresh or a shared link.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the address bar must keep the URL the reader asked for,
# because expo-router reads it to decide what to render. A redirect would rewrite
# it to / and lose the record.
#
# This does not swallow /data/*.json. Cloudflare Pages matches a static asset
# before it evaluates _redirects, which is the same precedence vercel.json relies
# on for its rewrite — and the reason the standard SPA splat is safe to use on a
# site that also serves real files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not here: the redirect from wikifoodia.pages.dev to the canonical .app host.
#
# It was tried here first and does not work. Cloudflare Pages ignores a hostname
# in the source of a _redirects rule -- the syntax is Netlify-compatible and this
# is exactly where the two differ. Deployed and measured: pages.dev still answered
# 200 with the page, not a 301.
#
# A Pages Function would work, and would route every request through the Worker,
# including the 2.3 MB catalogue, against a 100,000/day free limit. Not worth it
# for a redirect. It is done in the client instead -- see scripts/inject-canonical.mjs.
/*  /index.html  200
